# What the build of the Dockerfile next to this file takes from its context.
# Docker reads it because it carries that Dockerfile's name.
#
# Nothing, except what is listed: a file that appears in the repository (a
# local config with its keys, say) stays out of the image unless it is named
# here.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!lib/
!gfe/
!hack/loadtest/
!distribution/systemd/gfe-node.service
!prebuilt/
**/target/
